WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.010
A short surah of the Qur'an
begins: Say: He is Allah,

2
00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:06.910
the One and Only.

3
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.410
Many Muslims call it
a third of the Qur'an,

4
00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:13.290
because it sums up Tawhid: Allah is one.

5
00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:16.890
Another verse says no
vision can grasp Him.

6
00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:21.830
Yet the Qur'an also says: We are
nearer to him than his jugular vein.

7
00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:26.720
So how can Allah be beyond everything,
yet nearer than your own pulse?

8
00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:31.020
In this mission, you'll build a wheel
of the qualities Muslims give to Allah,

9
00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:33.510
from all-powerful to merciful.

10
00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:39.290
Then you'll weigh up a claim: that Allah
cannot be both transcendent and immanent.

11
00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:44.160
Your mission: find out how Muslims
believe Allah can be beyond everything,

12
00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.210
yet nearer than a jugular vein.
